The chips say what the session will be — where it runs, on what model,
under which permissions. Attaching a file is not one of those; it is
something done to the prompt, so it belongs at the other end of the
foot, next to the button that sends it.

A paperclip rather than a ⊕, which read as "another chip", and ⌘U as
well as the click. The shortcut is asked for rather than assumed: the
listener is on the window, and the chat panel is mounted once per tab,
so every hidden one would answer the keystroke with a file dialog of
its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
